<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP dependency-check suppressions for ShopFast.

  POLICY — read before adding anything here.

  This file is INTENTIONALLY EMPTY. The security gate fails the build on any
  dependency with CVSS >= 9, and the correct response to such a finding is to
  UPGRADE THE DEPENDENCY, not to silence the report. Suppressing a real critical
  vulnerability to make a pipeline green defeats the purpose of having the gate.

  A suppression is acceptable ONLY when all of the following hold, and each entry
  MUST carry a comment recording them:

    1. The finding is a demonstrable FALSE POSITIVE (e.g. dependency-check
       mismatched the CPE and attributed another product's CVE to this jar), or
       the vulnerable code path is provably unreachable in this application.
    2. No fixed version exists yet upstream.
    3. The entry names the specific CVE. Never suppress by broad regex, and
       never suppress an entire dependency.
    4. It carries an expiry date ("until") so it is re-examined rather than
       forgotten.

  Example of an acceptable entry (commented out — not active):

    <suppress until="2026-12-31Z">
      <notes>
        False positive: CPE matcher attributes jackson-core CVEs to
        jackson-databind. Tracked upstream at <issue link>.
      </notes>
      <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.example/some-lib@.*$</packageUrl>
      <cve>CVE-0000-00000</cve>
    </suppress>

  Current state: no suppressions. The CVEs that failed the previous run were
  resolved by upgrading Spring Boot 3.3.5 -> 3.5.6, which ships patched
  jackson-databind and log4j.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
</suppressions>
